{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller","id":1483236,"title":"Good One off chornicle ideas for inexperienced Storyteller/","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-06T11:15:54-07:00","id":1483236,"title":"Good One off chornicle ideas for inexperienced Storyteller/","content":"Like the title said, I'm a VERY green Storyteller (and even MORE green player) I ran a Chronicle over a decade ago in my (now gone) Wargaming club, and it did not go the best. <br /> <br /> I'd really like to get started again but have some obstacles. One, as a storyteller (or gm) I frequently made the mistake of planning big (or bigger than a one-shot) chronicles and had trouble keeping players. Some lost interest and some lost their availability. <br /> <br /> I know I mentioned in other posts that I'm thinking of a city campaign with potential for crossovers, but that's something I'm percolating in my head FIRST, I'd like to try a brief, one-shot story to get my toes wet, but I'm struggling. <br /> <br /> What would you do for a one shot Requiem chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T11:19:49-07:00","id":1483238,"title":"","content":"Depending on the length*, You can't go wrong with Reap the Whirlwind, a story centered on a city slipping into chaos after the PCs killed the former Prince-you can find it on DTRPG. Otherwise, a good murder mystery hits a lot of the things that Requiem does well, and usually tailors neatly to a night of gameplay.<br /> <br /> *You can play Reap the Whirlwind in an session, but it is a wee bit hefty, so if it's a shorter session, murder mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-06-2022, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T21:07:49-07:00","id":1483277,"title":"","content":"So I got &quot;Reap The Whirlwind, and I really, really like the beginning with the simplified character creator chapter. I wish the 2nd Edition book started like this. <br /> <br /> But I'm confused. The adventure suggests the players start as Ancillae vampires at least, so why only list the first two ranks for each discipline? Surely at the Ancillae phase you'd have at least ONE rank three discipline, wouldn't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T22:55:01-07:00","id":1483285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483277#post1483277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I got &quot;Reap The Whirlwind, and I really, really like the beginning with the simplified character creator chapter. I wish the 2nd Edition book started like this.<br /> <br /> But I'm confused. The adventure suggests the players start as Ancillae vampires at least, so why only list the first two ranks for each discipline? Surely at the Ancillae phase you'd have at least ONE rank three discipline, wouldn't you?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Convenience/space limitations because it was supposed to be a quickstart with ensuing copypasta update hiccups, i guess?<br /> <br /> Also, while all written for 1st edition, i think at least a few of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Storytelling_Adventure_System\" target=\"_blank\">published SAS stories</a> might be of interest for you in jumpstarting ideas.<br /> <br /> (In fact i guess &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot; might be somewhat inspired, if not an outright sequel to &quot;I<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Into_the_Void\" target=\"_blank\">nto the Void</a>&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-07-2022, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T23:30:45-07:00","id":1483289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483285#post1483285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Convenience/space limitations because it was supposed to be a quickstart with ensuing copypasta update hiccups, i guess?<br /> <br /> Also, while all written for 1st edition, i think at least a few of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Storytelling_Adventure_System\" target=\"_blank\">published SAS stories</a> might be of interest for you in jumpstarting ideas.<br /> <br /> (In fact i guess &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot; might be somewhat inspired, if not an outright sequel to &quot;I<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Into_the_Void\" target=\"_blank\">nto the Void</a>&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Into the Void is the story half of Reap the Whirlwind, RtW being the Second Edition Requiem Demo, chosen (if I recall correctly) because it spoke to how Requiem was no longer metaphorically waking up in Masquerade's bed by starting on the antithesis to the most common Masquerade chronicle (being &quot;kill the Prince&quot;, which....yeah, a story about how everything goes to shit when that happens is pretty much the game development equivalent of not giving a fuck when you drive past your ex.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-07-2022, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T05:03:16-07:00","id":1483299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483289#post1483289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Into the Void is the story half of Reap the Whirlwind, RtW being the Second Edition Requiem Demo, chosen (if I recall correctly) because it spoke to how Requiem was no longer metaphorically waking up in Masquerade's bed by starting on the antithesis to the most common Masquerade chronicle (being &quot;kill the Prince&quot;, which....yeah, a story about how everything goes to shit when that happens is pretty much the game development equivalent of not giving a fuck when you drive past your ex.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to know it wasn't my imagination, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> And before i forget, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?src=also_purchased&amp;filters=500_0_500_44499_0&amp;manufacturers_id=5573\" target=\"_blank\">another</a> &quot;old&quot; one.<br /> <br /> In fact i suspect that putting together the demo adventures of the multiple nWoD titles could provide quite decent fodder with which to season one's own flavor of chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-07-2022, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:55:03-07:00","id":1483421,"title":"","content":"I always recommend <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/24518/The-Resurrectionists-Vampire-The-Requiem?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Resurrectionists</b></a>: The player characters are tasked with body retrieval in a cemetery, which as archetypal a vampire story as it gets. It's got a simple hook, and the payoff is a great jumping off point for a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T18:12:32-07:00","id":1483427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483421#post1483421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always recommend <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/24518/The-Resurrectionists-Vampire-The-Requiem?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Resurrectionists</b></a>: The player characters are tasked with body retrieval in a cemetery, which as archetypal a vampire story as it gets. It's got a simple hook, and the payoff is a great jumping off point for a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, i love that one too. If memory tricks me not the major NPC in that one, Raphael Pope, makes a comeback in one of the Wicked Dead books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T22:02:12-07:00","id":1483442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483427#post1483427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, i love that one too. If memory tricks me not the major NPC in that one, Raphael Pope, makes a comeback in one of the Wicked Dead books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rafael Pope gets into all kinds of trouble in <b>Immortal Sinners</b>. I seem to recall that both the Unholy <i>and </i>Solomon Birch are gunning for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T04:02:36-07:00","id":1483451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483236-good-one-off-chornicle-ideas-for-inexperienced-storyteller?p=1483442#post1483442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rafael Pope gets into all kinds of trouble in <b>Immortal Sinners</b>. I seem to recall that both the Unholy <i>and </i>Solomon Birch are gunning for him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, that's just the intro to the book, that could be seen as a play on Ressurectionists, might be said.<br /> There's even more stuff inside on him, done to him and by him inside, but no spoilers, better to see on one's own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-09-2022, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}